---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const { user } = Astro.locals;
---
<Layout title="About this demo — Fern" navVariant="public" user={user} narrow>
  <div class="wrap-narrow stack-lg">
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">About this demo</span>
      <h1>A demonstration, not yet operating</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is the Fern patient zone, shown end to end on dummy data so the
        experience can be walked and reviewed. It is not live care.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="card stack">
      <h2>What is real, and what is not</h2>
      <p class="muted">
        The patient and clinician journeys are real and fully wired: account and
        identity, the two-lane intake, the clinician review and consult, payment,
        booking, the video room, dispensing status and membership. You can walk
        every happy and unhappy path.
      </p>
      <p class="muted">
        The regulated clinical core (the medical record and real prescribing)
        is deliberately a mock. No medicine is prescribed, no script is sent to a
        real pharmacy, and no real patient data exists here. Where external
        services are switched on, they run in test mode only.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="panel stack">
      <h3>No real patients, no live care</h3>
      <p class="muted">
        Fern delivers care only once registered to do so. Nothing here is medical
        advice. If you need urgent help, contact your GP or NHS 111, or call 999
        in an emergency.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="/demo" class="btn btn-pri">Pick a path and walk it</a>
      <a href="/" class="btn btn-ghost">Enter the demo from the start</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
</style>
